        "original_id": "7ad494e4-6fc5-57de-a581-83c3e97555c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Schuyler, H. G. Wells, Darragh Park\n- Works: The Morning of the Poem, The Time Machine, The Island of Doctor Moreau, The Invisible Man, The War of the Worlds, Love and Mr Lewisham\n- Awards: Pulitzer Prize for Poetry\n- Roles: literary executor\n\nFacts:\n- H. G. Wells wrote the science fiction works The Time Machine (1895), The Island of Doctor Moreau (1896), The Invisible Man (1897), and The War of the Worlds (1898).\n- H. G. Wells wrote Love and Mr Lewisham, a 1900 novel subtitled \"The Story of a Very Young Couple\" and set in the 1880s.\n- James Schuyler won the Pulitzer Prize for Poetry for his 1980 collection The Morning of the Poem.\n- Darragh Park (July 24, 1939 – April 17, 2009) was an American artist and the literary executor of James Schuyler's estate.",
